Subject: [PATCH] hk/tests: match agx_bo_bind's size_t parameter

The OOM test declares its wrapper with __typeof__(agx_bo_bind), but its
implementation used uint64_t for size. Those types differ on i686.
Use the production prototype's size_t; the mock's behavior is unchanged.
Keep this test-only backport until the pinned source includes the fix.

Source: https://github.com/aurora-silicon/mesa/blob/108c7218bbb6cddcb91c29680ff0770d29afcecc/src/asahi/vulkan/tests/test-hk-memory-oom.c

--- a/src/asahi/vulkan/tests/test-hk-memory-oom.c
+++ b/src/asahi/vulkan/tests/test-hk-memory-oom.c
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@
 
 int
 __wrap_agx_bo_bind(struct agx_device *dev, struct agx_bo *bo, uint64_t address,
-                   uint64_t size, uint64_t offset, uint32_t flags)
+                   size_t size, uint64_t offset, uint32_t flags)
 {
    return bind_fails ? -1 : 0;
 }
